<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      macVNC bundles Homebrew dylibs (libvncserver, OpenSSL libssl/libcrypto,
      libjpeg, libpng) under Contents/Frameworks. Under Developer ID hardened
      runtime, library validation breaks libvncserver's OpenSSL-backed VNC DES
      password check (observed as "password check failed" / INIT_FAILED).

      VERIFIED EMPIRICALLY (A/B on one and the same bundle, re-signed twice):
        without this entitlement -> INIT_FAILED, server log:
            "rfbAuthProcessClientMessage: password check failed"
        with this entitlement    -> AUTH_OK
      This holds EVEN THOUGH make_release.sh re-signs every bundled dylib with
      our own Developer ID (TeamIdentifier=GZL949D756 on all five), so the
      common assumption "sign the dylibs with the same team and the entitlement
      becomes unnecessary" is FALSE here. Do not remove it without re-running
      that A/B test with the reference libvncclient (vncdotool reports a false
      AUTH OK and must not be used to validate this).

      Residual risk accepted: an attacker who can already write into the
      installed bundle could substitute a dylib. Mitigation is bundle integrity
      (install location permissions), not this flag.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
